# Husky hooks must check out with LF: Git for Windows cannot spawn a CRLF,
# shebang-less hook ("cannot spawn .husky/pre-commit: Exec format error"),
# which silently breaks every commit. The index already stores them as LF —
# this rule stops the autocrlf smudge from re-corrupting working copies on
# checkout/merge. Scoped to .husky/ on purpose; broader rules (e.g. *.sh)
# would re-flag unrelated files across existing working trees.
.husky/** text eol=lf

# Same hazard, same narrow scoping: CI shell scripts run under `bash` on the
# Linux runner (safe — the index is LF) but are also meant to be runnable
# locally, which on Windows means the autocrlf smudge hands bash a CRLF file
# and every line ends in $'\r'. This path is new, so no existing working tree
# gets re-flagged.
.github/scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
